@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080/api


### 0a. See what categories already exist
GET {{base}}/part-categories

### 0b. See what bikes already exist
GET {{base}}/bikes
### 1. Create a category and a bike
POST {{base}}/part-categories
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Brakes" }

###
POST {{base}}/bikes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Splendor" }

### 2. SRS §7.2 example: MRP 500, discount 10%
POST {{base}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Brake Pad", "unit": "Pcs", "partCategoryId": 1, "bikeIds": [1],
  "itemType": "MRP", "mrp": 500.00, "defaultDiscountPercent": 10.00 }

### 3. Cash price -> expect rate 450.00
GET {{base}}/pricing/quote?itemId=2&customer=CASH

### 4. SRS §8.2: Cash discount 10 -> 15, permanently
POST {{base}}/pricing/permanent-changes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": 1, "customer": "CASH", "field": "DISCOUNT_PERCENT", "newValue": 15.00 }

### 5. Cash price -> expect 425.00 (source CASH_OVERRIDE)
GET {{base}}/pricing/quote?itemId=1&customer=CASH

### 6. Try to change the type -> expect 409 ITEM_TYPE_LOCKED
PUT {{base}}/items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Brake Pad", "unit": "Pcs", "partCategoryId": 1, "bikeIds": [1],
  "itemType": "NET_RATE", "defaultNetRate": 450.00 }

### 7. Remove the override, then retry step 6 -> expect 200
DELETE {{base}}/items/1/rate-overrides

### 8. Retry the type change -> now succeeds
PUT {{base}}/items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Brake Pad", "unit": "Pcs", "partCategoryId": 1, "bikeIds": [1],
  "itemType": "NET_RATE", "defaultNetRate": 450.00 }

### 9. Permanent delete, then confirm it's gone
DELETE {{base}}/items/1

###
GET {{base}}/items/1


###
POST {{base}}/pricing/permanent-changes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": 2, "customer": "CASH", "field": "DISCOUNT_PERCENT", "newValue": 20.00 }